<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naxalites</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1967">1967</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Naxalite movement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Naxalites are Maoist communist insurgents in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, named after the village of Naxalbari in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, where a peasant uprising broke out in 1967. Inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>'s doctrine of rural people's war, the movement split into many factions; the largest, the Communist Party of India (Maoist), formed in 2004, fought a long insurgency in the forested tribal districts of central and eastern India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naxalites.jpg" alt="Naxalites" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: .mw-parser-output .ubx-floatdefault[dir=&quot;ltr&quot;],.mw-parser-output .ubx-floatopposite[dir=&quot;rtl&quot;],.mw-parser-output .ubx... · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_Communism_Waving_Flag_Icon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
